    "result": "I implemented `check_password` in `solution.py` following the spec. I didn't run or test it, since shell access wasn't available.\n\n- **Type check:** It raises `TypeError` if the password or username isn't a `str`.\n- **LENGTH:** The length must be 12 to 64 characters inclusive.\n- **CLASSES:** The password needs characters from at least 3 of the 4 classes. Anything outside ASCII letters and digits, including `é`, counts as \"other\".\n- **USERNAME:** This is violated only when the username has 3 or more characters and its lowercase form appears in the lowercased password.\n- **REPEAT:** This is violated when the same character appears 3 or more times in a row. The comparison is case-sensitive.\n- **BLOCKLIST:** This is violated only when the lowercased password equals a lowercased blocklist entry. It ignores any non-string blocklist entries.\n\nViolations come back in the required order: `LENGTH`, `CLASSES`, `USERNAME`, `REPEAT`, `BLOCKLIST`.",
